<h2>1. Information on this website</h2>
<p>
  We try to keep the information on this website correct and up to date, but we
  do not guarantee that it is complete or free of errors. Programme plans and
  targets (such as planting 10,000 trees) describe goals, not results already
  achieved. Updates from the field describe work done on the dates shown.
</p>

<h2>2. Registration and tax benefits</h2>
<p>
  <%= trust.name %> will issue tax-exemption receipts under Section 80G of the
  Income Tax Act only after it receives 80G approval. Until then, donations do
  not carry any promised tax benefit. Temple Fund donations are generally not
  eligible for 80G even after approval. Please check with your tax adviser.
  The Trust does not accept foreign contributions.
</p>

<h2>3. Medical help</h2>
<p>
  The Trust is not a hospital or medical provider and does not give medical
  advice. Financial help for treatment, and medical camps run by the Trust,
  depend on verification and available funds, and are not guaranteed.
</p>

<h2>4. Collecting money in the Trust's name</h2>
<p>
  The Trust takes online donations only through this website. For cash or
  other payments, ask for a receipt signed by a trustee. If someone asks you for
  money in the Trust's name and you are unsure, call or WhatsApp us on
  <a href="tel:+91<%= trust.phone %>"><%= trust.phoneDisplay %></a> before paying.
</p>

<h2>5. External links and services</h2>
<p>
  Payments are processed by PayU, emails are sent through Gmail, and chats
  happen on WhatsApp. The Trust is not responsible for their content,
  availability or privacy practices.
</p>

<h2>6. Independence</h2>
<p>
  <%= trust.name %> is an independent charitable trust. It is not linked to
  any company (including Venturecore Solutions Pvt Ltd), political party or
  government body.
</p>

